# Works in Visual Studio 2022 (17.8+) and in VS Code (REST Client extension).
# Start the service first (docker compose up --build  OR  dotnet run --project src/ClaimsService).
# Auth:Mode=Disabled: X-Dev-User / X-Dev-Roles choose who you are (default dev-user with CLIENT,ADMIN).

@host = http://localhost:5081

### Health (is the database reachable?)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### 1) A customer submits a claim (UC-2). Status SUBMITTED, claim.submitted.v1 is published.
POST {{host}}/claims
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: c-ana
X-Dev-Roles: CLIENT
X-Dev-Email: ana@horica.test

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-1001",
  "incidentDate": "2026-11-01",
  "amount": 1200.00,
  "description": "Another driver reversed into my parked car. Rear bumper dented.",
  "documents": ["damage-photo-rear.jpg", "european-accident-report.pdf"],
  "type": "CAR"
}

### 2) The customer's claims (only their own)
GET {{host}}/claims
X-Dev-User: c-ana
X-Dev-Roles: CLIENT

### 3) One claim (replace the id with the one returned above)
GET {{host}}/claims/CLM-1001
X-Dev-User: c-ana
X-Dev-Roles: CLIENT

### 4) Pretend AgentService answered (Development only). 1.200 € > 300 € -> NEEDS_REVIEW, review.requested.v1
POST {{host}}/dev/claims/CLM-1001/recommendation
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Roles: REVIEWER

{
  "recommendation": "APPROVE",
  "summary": "Policy valid, photo and accident report attached. Amount is above the automatic limit.",
  "riskScore": 0.45,
  "riskReasons": ["Amount is 6 % of the policy limit"],
  "policyValid": true,
  "documentsComplete": true
}

### 5) Pretend ReviewService answered (Development only): Approved | Rejected | NeedsMoreInfo
POST {{host}}/dev/claims/CLM-1001/review-completed
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Roles: REVIEWER

{
  "decision": "NeedsMoreInfo",
  "reason": "Please add the repair shop's estimate.",
  "reviewerName": "marko"
}

### 6) Pretend DocumentService answered (Development only). On NEEDS_INFO this starts a re-analysis (UC-7).
POST {{host}}/dev/claims/CLM-1001/documents
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Roles: REVIEWER

{
  "names": ["repair-estimate.pdf"]
}

### 7) Employees: every claim, or only those waiting for a review
GET {{host}}/claims?status=NEEDS_REVIEW
X-Dev-Roles: REVIEWER

### 8) History of one claim (customers see fewer entries than employees)
GET {{host}}/claims/CLM-1001/history
X-Dev-Roles: REVIEWER

### 9) Managers: the audit log of every claim (UC-8)
GET {{host}}/claims/history
X-Dev-Roles: ADMIN

### A small claim with documents is approved automatically after the recommendation
POST {{host}}/claims
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: c-ana
X-Dev-Roles: CLIENT

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-1001",
  "incidentDate": "2026-11-05",
  "amount": 180,
  "description": "Small stone chip in the windscreen, repaired at a glass service.",
  "documents": ["windscreen-photo.jpg", "glass-repair-invoice.pdf"]
}
